        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: keep private memory out of shared sessions by default",
        "body": "Closes #84466\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes a privacy boundary bug where shared group, channel, scheduled, or delegated team-operation sessions could receive private long-term workspace memory by default when their session key or persisted metadata looked like a private/direct session.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe change centralizes the long-term memory default policy around canonical session classification and persisted policy stamps, then routes bootstrap loading, memory tools, transcript rotation, compaction, ACP/MCP/plugin tool contexts, scheduled/continuation runs, media/context-engine paths, and memory promotion through that boundary.\n\nPrivate/direct agent use keeps the documented default include behavior. Shared surfaces default to explicit-only memory unless they reach an allowed on-demand path.\n\nNon-goals: no new config knob, no version/release/changelog change, and no UI or visual changes.\n\nOwner review: this is security/privacy-sensitive session and memory behavior; please include the normal security/privacy and session-state owner review before taking it out of draft.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrivate long-term memory is no longer injected into shared/group/channel/team-operation sessions by default.\n\nShared transcripts keep their restrictive stamp through reset, compaction, continuation, tool inventory/invocation, MCP attach lifecycle, and scheduled/operator reconstruction paths. A later private/direct turn rotates to a fresh private transcript instead of mixing private memory into an explicit-only transcript.\n\nDirect/private sessions retain the existing documented behavior, including default long-term memory inclusion and explicit on-demand memory interactions where allowed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Local focused final-head proof on fb16e9aa06d3dcbf86ccdd1ec4d5314b61e79cec: ACP initialization/runtime handle regressions plus gateway MCP regressions passed.\n- Local generated/docs/type proof on final head: config baseline, plugin SDK API baseline, plugin SDK exports, plugin SDK surface report, docs map, docs MDX, docs formatting, prompt snapshots, plugin SDK declaration build, and diff whitespace checks all passed.\n- Fresh local autoreview at extra-high reasoning against origin/main: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Remote Testbox-through-Crabbox proof: tbx_01kwj8v6twg1ebjgnpq7cx1hk7, provider blacksmith-testbox, exact branch ref codex/memory-privacy-boundary, remote HEAD fb16e9aa06d3dcbf86ccdd1ec4d5314b61e79cec. Passed 11 Vitest shards plus generated/docs/type checks, prompt snapshots, plugin SDK declaration build, and diff whitespace checks. Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28620033391\n\nAI-assisted under maintainer direction.\n",
